{"unit":37,"section":2,"cefr":"A1","objective":"describe relationships","skill":"People","heading":"Describe relationships","phrases":[{"he":"אתה חבר שלי!","en":"You are my friend.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/c647455b6d8ae6e43bbabc0836ac5276","tokens":[{"w":"אתה","h":["you are","you"]},{"w":"חבר","h":["friend","boyfriend","a member"]},{"w":"שלי","h":["my","mine"]}]},{"he":"יש לנו מערכת יחסים טובה.","en":"We have got a good relationship.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/bc1de57f29216835169de786daf84d34","tokens":[{"w":"יש","h":["we have","have","there are","has"]},{"w":"לנו","h":["we have","to us","us","for us"]},{"w":"מערכת","h":["relationship","a system","system"]},{"w":"יחסים","h":["relationship"]},{"w":"טובה","h":["good (sg. fem.)","a favor","favor"]}]},{"he":"מי זה הבחור הזה?","en":"Who is that guy?","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/ceaf8b0cdb95fe52c7c13d09efac4667","tokens":[{"w":"מי","h":["who is","who","the one who"]},{"w":"זה","h":["this is","this","it is"]},{"w":"הבחור","h":["the young man","the guy","the boy"]},{"w":"הזה","h":["this","that"]}]},{"he":"אנחנו זוג.","en":"We are a couple.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/aba7481b900ec07580179f8a5dbf10d2","tokens":[{"w":"אנחנו","h":["we are","we"]},{"w":"זוג","h":["a couple","couple","a pair"]}]}],"words":[{"he":"זוג","en":"a couple","alt":["a pair","couple"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"חבר","en":"friend","alt":["a member","boyfriend"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"מערכת","en":"relationship","alt":["a system","system"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"יחסים","en":"relationship","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"הבחור","en":"the boy","alt":["the guy","the young man"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"בת","en":"daughter","alt":["the cousin","the female cousin","years old (sg. fem.)"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"בן","en":"boy","alt":["my partner","son","years old (sg. masc.)"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"הציבור","en":"the public","alt":[],"from":"skill"},{"he":"הישראלי","en":"the israeli","alt":[],"from":"skill"},{"he":"אתה","en":"you are","alt":["you"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"שלי","en":"my","alt":["mine"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"יש","en":"we have","alt":["have","there are","has"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"לנו","en":"we have","alt":["to us","us","for us"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"טובה","en":"favor","alt":["good (sg. fem.)","a favor"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"מי","en":"who is","alt":["who","the one who"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"זה","en":"this","alt":["this is","it is"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"הזה","en":"that","alt":["this"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"אנחנו","en":"we are","alt":["we"],"from":"phrase"}],"lexemes":["בת","בן","בני","בנות","צרפתים","חבֵרה","צרפתי","הציבור","מערכת היחסים","אוסטרלי","והבחורה","ידיד","ידידות","האוסטרלי","בקרן","הקרן","הבחור","בחורה","נערים","הקורבן","ישראלים","ישראלי","בני האדם","אנגלי","אזרחים","אזרח","ועדה","בוועדה","לפרט","ישראלית","אזרחי","הפרט","הנוער","אנגליה","האנגלי","הישראלי","הוועדה","בני אדם","בן אדם","לנוער"],"tips":"ידיד vs חבר\n----------\n\nIn Hebrew a חבר can be both a friend and a boyfriend, depending on the context. The same goes for חברה: friend and girlfriend. To avoid confusion, you may use the word ידיד/ה, which serves as \"platonic friend\".\nUsually, when one gender calls the other gender \"חבר / חברה\" this means they are in a relationship.\nFor example, a boy will call his male friend \"חבר\" but his female friend - ידידה. If he calls a girl \"חברה\", it usually means she's his girlfriend - and vice versa. **Try to use the word חבר/חברה carefully in order to prevent embarrassment**\n\nמבוגר\n------------\nIn this lesson you will learn the word מבוגר. This word can be both **adult** and **old** depending on the context. If it is functioning as a noun, it will necessarily be translated as \"adult\".\n\nThe \"old\" translation only applies to animate objects (like \"זקן\" does) - for example -  old people, old man, old dog.\nWe usually use this version when we want to say that a person is not too old (because calling someone זקן can sometimes sound insulting).\nSo try not to call old people \"זקן\" directly - using \"מבוגר\" is much more proper."}